# Hybrid prefill (0037): the grouped-GEMM gather runs over the FILLED pair
# count; a zero-resident batch takes the per-expert path
# (campaign: sub4bit-vram-kernel; the defect is in static-partition-prefill's
# patch 0037).
#
# Campaign: docs/campaigns/static-partition-prefill.md (status 2026-09-17)
#           docs/campaigns/sub4bit-vram-kernel.md (status 2026-09-17, night)
#
# The defect (measured, bisected): with the CPU tier under the static
# partition, the first prefill through exec_prefill_grouped_gemm page-faults
# on the Arc Pro B60 (Xe2): xe "Faulted Address ..., Fault response:
# Unsuccessful -ENOENT", a device coredump ("Timedout job", compute engine),
# CL_OUT_OF_RESOURCES from the runtime. Bisect on the served binary, the
# 35B at --offload-ratio 99 --moe-cpu-tier, one fresh process per cell:
# +p13 (through 0031) serves; +p16 (through 0037) faults; +p16 without 0037
# serves; +p17 with MOE_CPU_TIER_PARTITION=lru (0037's branch is
# static-partition-only) serves; the A770 (Xe-HPG) serves with 0037. Within
# 0037: disabling the post-GEMM host dispatch still faults; disabling the
# micro-GEMM remap still faults; disabling the grouped-GEMM remap serves; a
# zero-group guard alone still faults; a stream.finish() after every stage
# of the grouped path shows the first synchronisation, right after the
# gather, already throws.
#
# Mechanism: tokens_per_expert_cpu is created as token_num * max_topk entries
# of -1. Under 0037 only the RESIDENT (token, k) pairs are filled -- the
# non-resident pairs carry the sentinel and are skipped -- and the tail stays
# -1. The gather kernel (moe_gather_ref.cl, grouped mode) was still launched
# over total_gathered_tokens = token_num * max_topk, so every work-group past
# the fill computed token_index = -1 * HIDDEN_SIZE and read
# input[-HIDDEN_SIZE], one row before the activation buffer: unmapped on the
# B60 (the fault), mapped by luck on the A770 (silent). Before 0037 the
# static partition returned nullopt for any non-resident pair, so the fill
# was always complete and the launch size was right by accident.
#
# The fix: total_gathered_tokens = grouped_offsets_cpu[num_grouped_experts-1]
# (the filled count; exclusive end of the last slot), which also sizes the
# swiglu stage and the GEMM hint. And a guard: a batch whose routed experts
# are ALL non-resident (ratio 99: 6 of 128 slots) has nothing for the
# grouped GEMM and goes to the per-expert path, as it did before 0037.
#
# MEASURED (2026-09-17, B60, the served reproducer, plugin b05f8f1c = pin +
# 0003-0037 + this patch): the 35B serves Paris at ratio 99 with the tier,
# warm repeat identical, decode 23.6 t/s, prefill on the hybrid path; no
# fault, no coredump. Owed: a unit-ladder cell in moe_3gemm_gpu_test.cpp
# that builds the grouped tables with sentinel entries and asserts the
# filled count against the launch size (the served reproducer is the
# red-first cell of this patch; the unit cell is not written yet).
#
# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on
# top of patches/0003-0041.
#
# What changes:
#   moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp    build_grouped_mask_otd: zero-resident batch
#                                returns false (per-expert path).
#                                exec_prefill_grouped_gemm: total_gathered_tokens
#                                is the filled count.
#
--- a/src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/impls/ocl_v2/moe/moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/impls/ocl_v2/moe/moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp
@@ -1509,6 +1509,14 @@
             }
         }
 
+        // arcint (patch 0042). Under the static partition a batch can route to
+        // NO resident expert (ratio 99: 6 of 128 slots); the pre-0037 code
+        // returned nullopt for it and took the per-expert path, 0037 carried it
+        // into a grouped GEMM over ZERO groups, which page-faults on Xe2
+        // (bisected 2026-09-17, B60). Hand such a batch to the per-expert path.
+        if (num_actually_used_experts == 0)
+            return false;
+
         // Upload remapped topk_ids to GPU for scatter_reduce kernel
         auto& engine = instance.get_network().get_engine();
         size_t topk_bytes = topk_count * sizeof(uint32_t);
@@ -3226,7 +3234,14 @@
             }
         }
 
-        int total_gathered_tokens = static_cast<int>(token_num) * max_topk;
+        // arcint (patch 0042). Under the hybrid split (0037) the tables hold
+        // only the RESIDENT (token, k) pairs and the rest of
+        // tokens_per_expert_cpu stays -1. The gather, and everything sized by
+        // it, must run over the FILLED count, not token_num * max_topk: a
+        // work-group past the fill reads input[-HIDDEN_SIZE], one row before
+        // the activation buffer, which page-faults on Xe2 (bisected and
+        // stage-synchronised 2026-09-17, B60) and is silent on Xe-HPG.
+        int total_gathered_tokens = num_grouped_experts > 0 ? grouped_offsets_cpu[num_grouped_experts - 1] : 0;
 
         // Compute actual max tokens assigned to any single expert.
         int max_tokens_per_expert = 0;
